    summary: 'SEBI’s 23 November follow-up lists fake institutional and international-market pitches, unauthorised apps, third-party bank accounts and impersonated credentials. Use SEBI’s own registration, app and bank/UPI checks.',
    category: 'Markets', checkedAt: '2026-11-24', publishedAt: '2026-10-25', announcementDate: '2026-11-23', eventDate: '2026-11-23', dateLabel: 'Follow-up investor advisory issued', statusLabel: 'Investor advisory',
    updateNote: '24 November 2026: expanded the original 22 October guide with SEBI Press Release 76/2026, dated 23 November. The follow-up adds specific red flags for purported institutional/foreign-market opportunities, fake trading apps, third-party bank accounts, impersonated SEBI credentials and official verification tools. The October warning remains separately dated; this is an advisory, not a new trading rule.',
